            <ArticleTitle>Rapid evolution from coronary dissection to pseudoaneurysm after stent implantation: a glimpse at the pathogenesis using intravascular ultrasound.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>286-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary dissection during angioplasty can evolve into pseudoaneurysm. Stenting should prevent this complication. We present a case of coronary pseudoaneurysm after dissection that developed despite stent implantation. Intravascular ultrasound demonstrated no sealing of the false lumen due to undersizing and non-apposition to the wall by the stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
